WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.248 --> 00:00:04.081
- Hello Believe Nation.

00:00:04.081 --> 00:00:05.131
Today I'm going to talk about

00:00:05.131 --> 00:00:08.381
seven ways to get 10,000 Youtube views.

00:00:09.234 --> 00:00:12.237
♫ Nine, eight

00:00:12.237 --> 00:00:15.154
(electronic music)

00:00:16.979 --> 00:00:18.371
Alright so Youtube recently came out

00:00:18.371 --> 00:00:20.361
with a new policy that
if your channel did not

00:00:20.361 --> 00:00:23.500
have at least 10,000
lifetime Youtube views

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:24.356
on your channel

00:00:24.356 --> 00:00:27.139
then you would not get any monetization

00:00:27.139 --> 00:00:29.084
from Adsense on your channel.

00:00:29.084 --> 00:00:30.731
Once you crossed 10,000 views

00:00:30.731 --> 00:00:31.826
then you can start making money

00:00:31.826 --> 00:00:33.523
and so today I want to share with you

00:00:33.523 --> 00:00:37.149
my seven ways on how to
get that first 10,000 views

00:00:37.149 --> 00:00:38.767
for your channel.

00:00:38.767 --> 00:00:40.636
And for those of you who have
already hit the 10,000 views

00:00:40.636 --> 00:00:42.393
these strategies will help you too.

00:00:42.393 --> 00:00:44.893
(hiphop beat)

00:00:45.744 --> 00:00:48.893
Way number one is make a
video on a trending topic.

00:00:48.893 --> 00:00:51.623
Just kind of like what I'm
doing with this video right now.

00:00:51.623 --> 00:00:52.840
I'm eating my own dog food.

00:00:52.840 --> 00:00:55.244
This is a topic that a lot
of people are talking about.

00:00:55.244 --> 00:00:56.077
They're trying to figure out

00:00:56.077 --> 00:00:57.654
how do I get my first 10,000 views?

00:00:57.654 --> 00:00:58.763
And so what am I doing?

00:00:58.763 --> 00:01:01.325
Making a video about
something that's newsworthy

00:01:01.325 --> 00:01:02.453
and that people are talking about

00:01:02.453 --> 00:01:05.621
to help drive more traffic
and awareness on these videos.

00:01:05.621 --> 00:01:08.048
In general, this is not a
strategy that I usually do.

00:01:08.048 --> 00:01:10.315
Most of my content is evergreen content.

00:01:10.315 --> 00:01:13.351
Meaning, if you watch my
videos from five years ago

00:01:13.351 --> 00:01:15.167
it's still relevant, it's still applicable

00:01:15.167 --> 00:01:17.169
it's still helpful to you today.

00:01:17.169 --> 00:01:19.050
But it's not the strategy
that every Youtuber

00:01:19.050 --> 00:01:19.883
needs to go down

00:01:19.883 --> 00:01:22.118
or every content creator
needs to go down as well.

00:01:22.118 --> 00:01:24.401
So I'd be looking at, is
there anything in the news

00:01:24.401 --> 00:01:25.586
that you want to talk about?

00:01:25.586 --> 00:01:26.767
Whether it's politics.

00:01:26.767 --> 00:01:27.728
Whether it's business.

00:01:27.728 --> 00:01:29.097
Whether it's your local economy.

00:01:29.097 --> 00:01:31.937
Whatever it is, is there
something newsworthy

00:01:31.937 --> 00:01:33.153
that you have an opinion on

00:01:33.153 --> 00:01:34.618
that you want to share.

00:01:34.618 --> 00:01:36.087
When I was first staring with my agent

00:01:36.087 --> 00:01:37.414
he was always coaching me to say

00:01:37.414 --> 00:01:38.909
"I want you to take a powerful position

00:01:38.909 --> 00:01:40.951
"On this thing that is happening."

00:01:40.951 --> 00:01:45.586
This political scene or that
this company did this thing.

00:01:45.586 --> 00:01:46.985
And it was really hard for me

00:01:46.985 --> 00:01:48.897
because I don't really care.

00:01:48.897 --> 00:01:50.197
I don't really have strong opinions

00:01:50.197 --> 00:01:53.354
on politics and what else
is happening in the news.

00:01:53.354 --> 00:01:55.401
I don't really follow pop
culture, a lot of these things

00:01:55.401 --> 00:01:56.509
that people are concerned about.

00:01:56.509 --> 00:01:58.599
I don't really care about
most of the newsworthy

00:01:58.599 --> 00:01:59.965
buzzworthy things.

00:01:59.965 --> 00:02:01.486
And so I couldn't create content around it

00:02:01.486 --> 00:02:03.345
but it doesn't mean that you can't.

00:02:03.345 --> 00:02:04.798
And it's a powerful way to help you get

00:02:04.798 --> 00:02:06.571
your first 10,000 views.

00:02:06.571 --> 00:02:09.071
(hiphop beat)

00:02:10.425 --> 00:02:13.218
Way number two is to
create a reaction video.

00:02:13.218 --> 00:02:15.521
If you look at a video
that is already having

00:02:15.521 --> 00:02:16.745
a lot of success

00:02:16.745 --> 00:02:18.980
it's easy to piggyback off of that video

00:02:18.980 --> 00:02:20.435
by making a similar one

00:02:20.435 --> 00:02:22.192
with your own thoughts, your own opinions.

00:02:22.192 --> 00:02:24.329
So for example, if a
channel put out a video

00:02:24.329 --> 00:02:27.969
about the top seven marketing
books for entrepreneurs.

00:02:27.969 --> 00:02:29.818
If you had a thought on that

00:02:29.818 --> 00:02:31.942
you want to share your list
of books for entrepreneurs

00:02:31.942 --> 00:02:34.297
you can make a video with the same topic.

00:02:34.297 --> 00:02:37.160
The top seven books for
entrepreneurs in marketing.

00:02:37.160 --> 00:02:39.157
And then you can share
your thoughts right?

00:02:39.157 --> 00:02:40.628
It's not just copying
what somebody else did

00:02:40.628 --> 00:02:41.889
from the topic point of view

00:02:41.889 --> 00:02:43.775
but adding more context and clarity

00:02:43.775 --> 00:02:44.978
around your opinions of it.

00:02:44.978 --> 00:02:47.467
So the goal is, when
somebody watches that video

00:02:47.467 --> 00:02:50.576
yours is going to be the next
one that pops up right afterwards

00:02:50.576 --> 00:02:52.001
so if you use a similar title

00:02:52.001 --> 00:02:54.271
you use some of the same
words in the description

00:02:54.271 --> 00:02:55.694
you use similar tags

00:02:55.694 --> 00:02:56.927
then you're likely to show up

00:02:56.927 --> 00:02:58.793
after that first video.

00:02:58.793 --> 00:03:00.585
Just make sure again,
that you're adding value

00:03:00.585 --> 00:03:02.397
you're adding some context there

00:03:02.397 --> 00:03:04.144
or you're adding something
that's worth watching.

00:03:04.144 --> 00:03:05.592
You have something that you want to add

00:03:05.592 --> 00:03:06.569
your own opinion to

00:03:06.569 --> 00:03:08.002
and you're not just trying to piggyback

00:03:08.002 --> 00:03:09.647
off of somebody for the wrong reasons.

00:03:09.647 --> 00:03:11.446
There has to still be a good quality video

00:03:11.446 --> 00:03:13.942
but if you can create
a good reaction video

00:03:13.942 --> 00:03:15.311
or a good piggyback video

00:03:15.311 --> 00:03:17.676
then it's much easier to
get those initial views

00:03:17.676 --> 00:03:19.116
coming into your channel.

00:03:19.116 --> 00:03:21.616
(hiphop beat)

00:03:22.674 --> 00:03:25.406
Way number three is update
your social media bios.

00:03:25.406 --> 00:03:26.709
In most social media platforms

00:03:26.709 --> 00:03:28.866
you have an opportunity to put a link.

00:03:28.866 --> 00:03:30.463
Where is that link going?

00:03:30.463 --> 00:03:31.930
What you want to do

00:03:31.930 --> 00:03:33.681
is try to get as much
traffic and much attention

00:03:33.681 --> 00:03:35.856
going to your Youtube channel as possible.

00:03:35.856 --> 00:03:37.246
You want to hit that 10,000 views

00:03:37.246 --> 00:03:38.750
as quickly as possible.

00:03:38.750 --> 00:03:40.754
And so there's actually a cool tool

00:03:40.754 --> 00:03:41.587
out of TubeBuddy.

00:03:41.587 --> 00:03:42.611
TubeBuddy is a tool that I use.

00:03:42.611 --> 00:03:44.502
I don't know if this is part
of the free version or not.

00:03:44.502 --> 00:03:45.734
I'm not associated with the company

00:03:45.734 --> 00:03:47.994
apart from being a happy user.

00:03:47.994 --> 00:03:49.896
They have an option to have a link

00:03:49.896 --> 00:03:52.610
to your most recent Youtube video.

00:03:52.610 --> 00:03:55.450
And so right now, that's the
bio for my Twitter account.

00:03:55.450 --> 00:03:58.013
It's the bio for my Instagram account.

00:03:58.013 --> 00:04:00.823
It's the bio on my Facebook account.

00:04:00.823 --> 00:04:02.090
I don't think it's Linkedin.

00:04:02.090 --> 00:04:03.464
I've got to update my Linkedin account.

00:04:03.464 --> 00:04:05.910
So anytime somebody goes
to see my social media

00:04:05.910 --> 00:04:08.002
they see that link, they can click on it.

00:04:08.002 --> 00:04:10.054
It will take them to my most recent video.

00:04:10.054 --> 00:04:11.096
Even if you don't do that

00:04:11.096 --> 00:04:13.005
you can link them to a single video

00:04:13.005 --> 00:04:13.921
that you really want to promote

00:04:13.921 --> 00:04:15.823
or you can lead them to your channel

00:04:15.823 --> 00:04:16.907
that you really want to promote.

00:04:16.907 --> 00:04:20.119
Having that link, because most
of the time you get one link.

00:04:20.119 --> 00:04:21.400
Put it in there so that any time

00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:22.754
somebody checks you on social media

00:04:22.754 --> 00:04:25.038
they're also going to check
out your Youtube videos.

00:04:25.038 --> 00:04:27.498
As a side note, you can
also put it in your emails.

00:04:27.498 --> 00:04:29.383
At the bottom of my
emails in every signature

00:04:29.383 --> 00:04:31.401
it will say, "Here's a
link to my latest video."

00:04:31.401 --> 00:04:33.807
So that anytime you send
an email out to somebody

00:04:33.807 --> 00:04:36.448
you put it as a PS, just
have it as a default

00:04:36.448 --> 00:04:37.414
in your signature.

00:04:37.414 --> 00:04:39.205
You send out emails, people like it.

00:04:39.205 --> 00:04:40.294
Some are going to click through

00:04:40.294 --> 00:04:41.950
and you get more views on your channel.

00:04:41.950 --> 00:04:44.450
(hiphop beat)

00:04:45.755 --> 00:04:47.519
Number four is do some collabs.

00:04:47.519 --> 00:04:48.961
One of the best ways to grow a channel

00:04:48.961 --> 00:04:50.815
is to partner up and
collaborate with somebody

00:04:50.815 --> 00:04:53.198
who already has an audience
and channel of their own.

00:04:53.198 --> 00:04:54.808
It doesn't have to be a massive channel.

00:04:54.808 --> 00:04:57.361
But they have a similar sized channel

00:04:57.361 --> 00:04:58.744
or maybe slightly bigger than yours

00:04:58.744 --> 00:05:00.172
and you're giving them value

00:05:00.172 --> 00:05:01.783
that they can promote to their audience.

00:05:01.783 --> 00:05:03.823
You have a video on their channel now.

00:05:03.823 --> 00:05:04.932
People are going to learn about you.

00:05:04.932 --> 00:05:06.525
They're going to want to
say, "Hey who is that person?

00:05:06.525 --> 00:05:07.358
"What's their channel?

00:05:07.358 --> 00:05:08.191
"Let me check them out."

00:05:08.191 --> 00:05:09.259
And they're going to funnel your way.

00:05:09.259 --> 00:05:10.633
Some of the first collabs I did

00:05:10.633 --> 00:05:13.285
was with Youtubers Tim Schmoyer

00:05:13.285 --> 00:05:14.699
and Derral Eves.

00:05:14.699 --> 00:05:17.472
I've done four collabs
with stand alone videos

00:05:17.472 --> 00:05:18.305
I think with Tim.

00:05:18.305 --> 00:05:20.213
I was part of his Youtube
entrepreneur series

00:05:20.213 --> 00:05:21.807
that ran for 12 episodes.

00:05:21.807 --> 00:05:24.284
Derral I think we did one video together.

00:05:24.284 --> 00:05:25.718
And it was just basically finding ways

00:05:25.718 --> 00:05:28.042
that I could add value to their audience

00:05:28.042 --> 00:05:30.173
at the time they both had bigger audiences

00:05:30.173 --> 00:05:31.038
than I did.

00:05:31.038 --> 00:05:33.141
And so it really helped me
get some initial traffic

00:05:33.141 --> 00:05:34.266
and views on my channel.

00:05:34.266 --> 00:05:36.797
I've gone on to do a
lot more collaborations.

00:05:36.797 --> 00:05:38.685
We've had guests come on my channel.

00:05:38.685 --> 00:05:40.457
I've been on other people's channels.

00:05:40.457 --> 00:05:42.333
I did a series with Brian Tracy

00:05:42.333 --> 00:05:44.448
the sales and time management expert

00:05:44.448 --> 00:05:48.048
where we did the top 10
rules for entrepreneurs.

00:05:48.048 --> 00:05:49.781
Something like that, he
had five on his channel.

00:05:49.781 --> 00:05:51.329
I had five on my channel.

00:05:51.329 --> 00:05:52.735
At the end of our videos, we both said

00:05:52.735 --> 00:05:54.334
go check out the other person's channel

00:05:54.334 --> 00:05:55.811
to see the other five rules.

00:05:55.811 --> 00:05:57.190
So those kinds of things.

00:05:57.190 --> 00:05:59.782
Coming up with creative
ways to market yourself

00:05:59.782 --> 00:06:01.703
and work with other Youtube creators

00:06:01.703 --> 00:06:03.721
ideally somewhat in the same space

00:06:03.721 --> 00:06:07.378
so they have an audience that
is related to your audience.

00:06:07.378 --> 00:06:09.443
It's kind of the same base from.

00:06:09.443 --> 00:06:11.408
That they would want
to then check you out.

00:06:11.408 --> 00:06:13.971
If I look at Tim's
audience, Derral's audience

00:06:13.971 --> 00:06:14.804
as an example

00:06:14.804 --> 00:06:16.385
their audiences are all Youtubers.

00:06:16.385 --> 00:06:18.280
People who only want to build an income

00:06:18.280 --> 00:06:19.500
based off of Youtube.

00:06:19.500 --> 00:06:21.133
But they're all entrepreneurs

00:06:21.133 --> 00:06:23.645
so it's a subsegment
of my audience as well

00:06:23.645 --> 00:06:25.871
and so those collaborations
really did some work.

00:06:25.871 --> 00:06:27.833
So look at who is already in your market.

00:06:27.833 --> 00:06:29.852
Who is doing videos for an audience

00:06:29.852 --> 00:06:30.867
that is similar to yours

00:06:30.867 --> 00:06:33.042
and how can you find
a way to work together

00:06:33.042 --> 00:06:34.808
and give them value?

00:06:34.808 --> 00:06:37.308
(hiphop beat)

00:06:38.863 --> 00:06:40.906
Way number five is make a one word video.

00:06:40.906 --> 00:06:42.155
Now you may know what your one word is.

00:06:42.155 --> 00:06:43.180
You may know what you're all about.

00:06:43.180 --> 00:06:45.920
You may understand what your
you know, core value is.

00:06:45.920 --> 00:06:47.383
You may not know, and you
can check out the book

00:06:47.383 --> 00:06:48.216
if you want to.

00:06:48.216 --> 00:06:49.979
Even if you can't get it down to one word

00:06:49.979 --> 00:06:51.957
just understanding why you're here.

00:06:51.957 --> 00:06:53.498
It's making a why video.

00:06:53.498 --> 00:06:55.661
What is this channel all about?

00:06:55.661 --> 00:06:56.682
Why is it so important?

00:06:56.682 --> 00:06:58.727
And not just, not from
a mental point of view.

00:06:58.727 --> 00:07:01.577
Not from a here's why you need
to subscribe to my channel.

00:07:01.577 --> 00:07:03.055
Nobody really cares about those videos.

00:07:03.055 --> 00:07:05.220
But from the heart.

00:07:05.220 --> 00:07:07.625
Something coming out that you have made

00:07:07.625 --> 00:07:09.635
that you just think is awesome.

00:07:09.635 --> 00:07:11.629
The video that helped explode my channel

00:07:11.629 --> 00:07:13.321
the first video that really took off

00:07:13.321 --> 00:07:16.017
and got 100,000 views in the first month

00:07:16.017 --> 00:07:17.416
and now it's at two million views

00:07:17.416 --> 00:07:20.621
was Believe, it was a video about believe.

00:07:20.621 --> 00:07:22.455
When I watched it, it was like yes.

00:07:22.455 --> 00:07:23.365
That's what it's about.

00:07:23.365 --> 00:07:24.497
That's what I want people to feel

00:07:24.497 --> 00:07:26.197
when they come and visit my channel.

00:07:26.197 --> 00:07:28.132
That's what I want
entrepreneurs to look at

00:07:28.132 --> 00:07:29.955
on a regular basis and feel every day

00:07:29.955 --> 00:07:31.319
as they bring that to their business.

00:07:31.319 --> 00:07:34.302
So, a passionate why video

00:07:34.302 --> 00:07:36.783
for what you're doing here.

00:07:36.783 --> 00:07:38.327
Why is this so important to you.

00:07:38.327 --> 00:07:39.485
Something that when you watch it

00:07:39.485 --> 00:07:40.609
it gets your blood excited

00:07:40.609 --> 00:07:41.733
and say yes, that's it.

00:07:41.733 --> 00:07:43.100
That's the feeling I want people to feel.

00:07:43.100 --> 00:07:44.969
If you can pour that
kind of love and energy

00:07:44.969 --> 00:07:47.017
into making that kind of heroic video.

00:07:47.017 --> 00:07:48.012
Then you have a good chance

00:07:48.012 --> 00:07:49.782
of getting those first 10K views.

00:07:49.782 --> 00:07:52.282
(hiphop beat)

00:07:53.746 --> 00:07:56.029
Way number six is get
your friends to help.

00:07:56.029 --> 00:07:58.515
You have friends, let them
know about your channel

00:07:58.515 --> 00:07:59.507
and let them know about your mission.

00:07:59.507 --> 00:08:00.473
Let them know what you're trying to do.

00:08:00.473 --> 00:08:02.113
Let them know you're
trying to get to 10K views.

00:08:02.113 --> 00:08:03.442
Send them the videos

00:08:03.442 --> 00:08:05.240
that you feel are most relevant to them.

00:08:05.240 --> 00:08:06.073
That they would enjoy

00:08:06.073 --> 00:08:08.466
they find some value at,
that they may want to share

00:08:08.466 --> 00:08:10.245
and help other people with as well.

00:08:10.245 --> 00:08:12.452
I still use this strategy.

00:08:12.452 --> 00:08:14.293
As an example, when I was
trying to get interviews

00:08:14.293 --> 00:08:15.688
for your one word.

00:08:15.688 --> 00:08:17.264
I interviewed the Honest Company.

00:08:17.264 --> 00:08:18.923
And to get in the door

00:08:18.923 --> 00:08:20.982
I made a video on it

00:08:20.982 --> 00:08:22.797
and then I asked people to leave comments

00:08:22.797 --> 00:08:24.154
on the video

00:08:24.154 --> 00:08:27.122
to show that there was
engagement and action

00:08:27.122 --> 00:08:28.997
and then I could take
that to the Honest Company

00:08:28.997 --> 00:08:30.503
and say, "Hey look, people are curious.

00:08:30.503 --> 00:08:31.485
"People want to hear from you.

00:08:31.485 --> 00:08:32.644
"How about we set up a meeting

00:08:32.644 --> 00:08:34.801
"So that I can have you in my book?"

00:08:34.801 --> 00:08:37.961
And so where I got the
most results from that

00:08:37.961 --> 00:08:40.197
was actually my Facebook friends.

00:08:40.197 --> 00:08:41.739
I sent it to my Youtube audience.

00:08:41.739 --> 00:08:44.391
I sent out a couple of
newsletters to my newsletter list

00:08:44.391 --> 00:08:46.204
and said, "Hey guys, can
you support me in this?

00:08:46.204 --> 00:08:47.071
"Here's what I'm trying to do.

00:08:47.071 --> 00:08:48.574
"Can you please leave a
comment on this video?"

00:08:48.574 --> 00:08:51.851
But I got the best results
from my Facebook friends.

00:08:51.851 --> 00:08:53.501
Where I went down my entire list

00:08:53.501 --> 00:08:55.485
and I had a message and it said

00:08:55.485 --> 00:08:57.470
"Dear whoever, I'm trying to do this.

00:08:57.470 --> 00:08:58.999
"Can you please support me?

00:08:58.999 --> 00:09:01.515
"Watch this video, leave a comment on it.

00:09:01.515 --> 00:09:03.274
"It would really, really,
really mean a lot to me."

00:09:03.274 --> 00:09:05.688
That was the highest response rate

00:09:05.688 --> 00:09:07.129
and it lead to the most number of comments

00:09:07.129 --> 00:09:08.888
on that video.

00:09:08.888 --> 00:09:11.183
And so I wouldn't
underestimate your friends.

00:09:11.183 --> 00:09:12.978
I would look at the people
who you hang out with.

00:09:12.978 --> 00:09:14.410
It doesn't have to be your close friends.

00:09:14.410 --> 00:09:15.938
But friends of friends.

00:09:15.938 --> 00:09:18.455
People who you know, they
would recognize your name

00:09:18.455 --> 00:09:20.626
if you went off and
asked them for a favor.

